 "fx_ppp": {
  "_doc": "FX vs PPP (#1374, /v1/fx/ppp): spot = the latest ECB reference rate (em_bonds.fx, base USD, local currency per USD); PPP = the World Bank PPP conversion factor (PA.NUS.PPP, LCU per international $) of its latest year, carried to the latest year both the country and the US publish CPI (FP.CPI.TOTL) by relative inflation; over/under % = PPP / spot - 1 (negative: undervalued); window = the last window_days calendar days' average spot, and the same window 365 days earlier adjusted by the last year's CPI growth home vs US (the rate that leaves the real exchange rate unchanged); real change % = that / today's average - 1 (positive: the currency gained in real terms). The euro uses Germany's PPP and CPI (the World Bank publishes no euro-area PPP).",
