 "fx_matrix": {
  "_doc": "G20 FX & PPP Matrix (#1396, /v1/fx/ppp-matrix; supersedes the FX vs PPP note of #1374). Rates are local currency per USD (LCU/USD). today = the latest daily rate (ECB reference rates via em_bonds.fx; the rouble from the Bank of Russia, feeds.rub); ma_Ny = the window_days calendar-day average ending N*365 days before today's date, adjusted by RPPP S_hist*(1+pi_dom)/(1+pi_US) with pi the cumulative World Bank CPI (FP.CPI.TOTL) growth over the N years ending at the latest year both sides publish; macro_ppp = the World Bank PPP conversion factor (PA.NUS.PPP) carried to that CPI year by relative inflation (the fx_ppp maths); retail_ppp = The Economist Big Mac implied rate (local price / US price) of the latest survey; diff_x = today / x - 1 (%). DXY = constant * prod(LCU/USD ^ weight) over the ICE legs (the same as 50.14348112 * EURUSD^-0.576 * USDJPY^0.136 * GBPUSD^-0.119 * USDCAD^0.091 * USDSEK^0.042 * USDCHF^0.036), computed per column from the legs' values. The euro uses Germany's CPI and PPP (the World Bank publishes no euro-area PPP), the Big Mac euro-area price.",
