   }
  ],
  "method": "10Y nominal yield: 30-day moving average of the daily benchmark (US Treasury via FRED DGS10; the container's daily curve feeds: Bundesbank, MoF Japan, BoE, BoC, RBA), else the OECD monthly long-term rate (via DBnomics) for the month the window centres on. FX: ECB reference rates (Frankfurter), RUB from the Bank of Russia; US CPI: FRED CPIAUCSL.",
  "footer": "Pure fixed-rate nominal benchmarks (no inflation-linked debt; Brazil NTN-F, not NTN-B). FX depreciation = MA30 today / MA30 -1y - 1 (LCU per USD; + = local currency weaker); 3Y = (MA30 today / MA30 -3y)^(1/3) - 1. Net USD yield = nominal today - FX depreciation. Real = net - US CPI (trailing 12 months). All in % a year; a dash names its reason below."
 },
