  "_doc": "#1416 THE free, non-real-time data stack of FinTerm: five sources, each a declared store format of the container (capital-stack-finterminal-api, store.rs STORE_FORMATS; gen-fetchers.mjs checks this block) and a direct-fetch path in the APK (FreeStack.kt). About > Data sources (APK) and the web About page list every source here with its coverage, licence/terms, rate limit, key need and live status. Nothing about a source is typed in Kotlin, Rust or Svelte. per_min is the hard pacing budget (requests a minute, one gap of 60000/per_min ms between two requests to one source). A keyed source names its fleet secret (key.env: the container reads it from the fleet secret store through that variable, never prints it) and its APK key slot (key.slot, Config > Sources, encrypted on the phone); without a key the source reports needs_key with key.reason. A flagged source (flag) runs only when its flag is on (container env flag.env = 1; APK flag.default) and only as the last fallback after flag.after.",
